✅ Summary in Plain English
The recursive or() channel pattern:

Spins up a goroutine at each level of recursion (except base case).
That goroutine does a select on two or more channels.
As soon as any input channel receives a signal (i.e., is closed), the goroutine:
Closes its own orDone channel, signaling cancellation.
This closed orDone ripples back up to cancel all others